+<section>
+<h2>2. The Transfer Function — SLAU367P §34.2.1, Equation 13</h2>
+
+<p>TI's MSP430FR58xx/59xx family user's guide (SLAU367P) defines the ADC12_B conversion result in §34.2.1, Equation 13:</p>
+
+<div class="equation">
+  N<sub>ADC</sub> &nbsp;=&nbsp; <span class="fs">4095</span> &nbsp;×&nbsp;
+  <span class="frac">
+    <span class="top"><span class="vin">V<sub>in</sub></span> − <span class="vr">V<sub>R−</sub></span></span>
+    <span class="bot"><span class="vr">V<sub>R+</sub></span> − <span class="vr">V<sub>R−</sub></span></span>
+  </span>
+  <span class="eq-note">4095 = full-scale code for 12-bit mode; more generally FS = 2<sup>resolution</sup> − 1</span>
+</div>
+
+<ul>
+  <li><strong>V<sub>in</sub></strong> — the analog input voltage on the selected channel.</li>
+  <li><strong>V<sub>R+</sub></strong> — the positive reference: the voltage that maps to full scale. Selected by <code>ADC12VRSEL</code>.</li>
+  <li><strong>V<sub>R−</sub></strong> — the negative reference: the voltage that maps to code 0. In Silmulator's model it is fixed at AVSS (0 V), so the equation simplifies to <code>N = FS × Vin / VR+</code>.</li>
+  <li><strong>FS</strong> — the full-scale code: 4095 (12-bit), 1023 (10-bit), or 255 (8-bit), matching <code>ADC12RES</code>.</li>
+</ul>
+
+<h3>Worked example 1 — the probe case: 1.2 V input against the 1.2-V VREF</h3>
+<pre><code>N = 4095 × (1.2 − 0) / (1.2 − 0)
+  = 4095 × 1.0
+  = <span class="num">4095</span>   <span class="cm"># full scale — the input IS the reference</span></code></pre>
+
+<h3>Worked example 2 — the same 1.2 V input against AVCC = 3.3 V</h3>
