+<section>
+<h2>3. The Fix — What Commit 58b7e2d Actually Changed</h2>
+
+<p>Issue #18 came out of the MSP430 compliance audit (<code>docs/audits/msp430-compliance-report.md</code>). Two ADC families were NON_COMPLIANT for the same root cause: the model ignored the reference.</p>
+
+<h3>Before: a hardcoded 3.3 in the conversion path</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># silmulator/silmulator/devices/msp430.py — BEFORE 58b7e2d</span>
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_adc_ch_raw</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>, ac: <span class="cls">ADCChannel</span>) -> str:
+    <span class="del">return str(self.faults.adc_code(ac.value, 3.3, ac.resolution))</span>
+                                              <span class="cm"># ↑ VR+ frozen at 3.3 V forever</span></code></pre>
+
+<p>And <code>ADC:REFERENCE</code> stored <em>any</em> string without complaint — <code>ADC:REFERENCE BANANA</code> succeeded, and the stored value was never read by the conversion code. Two independent defects: <strong>no validation</strong> and <strong>no effect</strong>.</p>
+
+<h3>After: VR+ is resolved from the selected reference at conversion time</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># silmulator/silmulator/devices/msp430.py — AFTER 58b7e2d</span>
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_adc_ch_raw</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>, ac: <span class="cls">ADCChannel</span>) -> str:
+    <span class="add">return str(self.faults.adc_code(ac.value, self._adc_reference_voltage(), ac.resolution))</span>
+
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_adc_reference_voltage</span>(self) -> float:
+    <span class="str">"""VR+ in volts for the selected ADC reference (SLAU367P §34.2.1 Eq. 13).
+
+    VR- is AVSS (0 V) in this model — the simulator does not expose the
+    VR- half of ADC12VRSEL's combinations, only which source drives VR+.
+    """</span>
+    ref = self.adc[<span class="num">0</span>].reference
+    <span class="kw">if</span> ref == <span class="str">"AVCC"</span>:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> self.clock.vcc          <span class="cm"># reads CPU:VCC live — not a snapshot</span>
+    <span class="kw">if</span> ref == <span class="str">"VEREF"</span>:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> self._veref_v           <span class="cm"># the external VeREF+ pin voltage</span>
+    <span class="kw">return</span> ADC_INTERNAL_REF_V.get(ref, self.clock.vcc)  <span class="cm"># REF_A outputs</span></code></pre>
+
+<h3>The new module-level reference table</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># REF_A's three internal reference outputs (SLAU367P §33.3.1, REFVSEL field).</span>
+<span class="cm"># Bare "VREF" maps to REFVSEL's reset value (00b = 1.2 V).</span>
+ADC_INTERNAL_REF_V: <span class="cls">Dict</span>[str, float] = {
+    <span class="str">"VREF"</span>:    <span class="num">1.2</span>,
+    <span class="str">"VREF1.2"</span>: <span class="num">1.2</span>,
+    <span class="str">"VREF2.0"</span>: <span class="num">2.0</span>,
+    <span class="str">"VREF2.5"</span>: <span class="num">2.5</span>,
+}
+
+<span class="cm"># The fixed set ADC:REFERENCE accepts: AVCC (tracks CPU:VCC), REF_A's internal</span>
+<span class="cm"># outputs, and VEREF (the external VeREF+ pin). Anything else has no</span>
+<span class="cm"># ADC12VRSEL encoding and is rejected with -224.</span>
+VALID_ADC_REFERENCES = <span class="fn">frozenset</span>({<span class="str">"AVCC"</span>, <span class="str">"VEREF"</span>} | <span class="fn">set</span>(ADC_INTERNAL_REF_V))</code></pre>
+
+<h3>Validation in the SCPI handler</h3>
+<pre><code><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_adc_ref</span>(self, cmd: <span class="cls">ScpiCommand</span>) -> str:
+    <span class="kw">if</span> cmd.is_query:
+        <span class="kw">return</span> self.adc[<span class="num">0</span>].reference
+    <span class="kw">if</span> cmd.params:
+        ref = cmd.params[<span class="num">0</span>].upper()
+        <span class="kw">if</span> ref <span class="kw">not in</span> VALID_ADC_REFERENCES:
+            <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="cls">ScpiError</span>(-<span class="num">224</span>, f<span class="str">"Illegal ADC reference: {ref}"</span>)
+        <span class="kw">if</span> ref == <span class="str">"VEREF"</span> <span class="kw">and</span> len(cmd.params) > <span class="num">1</span>:
+            <span class="kw">try</span>:
+                self._veref_v = <span class="fn">float</span>(cmd.params[<span class="num">1</span>])
+            <span class="kw">except</span> <span class="cls">ValueError</span>:
+                <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="cls">ScpiError</span>(-<span class="num">104</span>, f<span class="str">"Invalid VEREF voltage: {cmd.params[1]}"</span>)
+        <span class="kw">for</span> ch <span class="kw">in</span> self.adc.values():
+            ch.reference = ref     <span class="cm"># one reference for all channels (single-VR+ model)</span>
+    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="str">""</span></code></pre>
+
+<h3>Tests flipped from expected-failure to passing</h3>
+<p>The two audit-derived tests dropped their <code>@pytest.mark.xfail(strict=True)</code> decorators — the code now does what SLAU367P says:</p>
+<pre><code><span class="cm"># tests/test_msp430_edge_cases.py — AFTER 58b7e2d (xfail decorators removed)</span>
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">test_reference_out_of_range_rejected</span>(self, mcu):
+    <span class="cm"># SLAU367P §34.2.4 (ADC12VRSEL), §33 (REF_A): the reference is selected</span>
+    <span class="cm"># from a fixed set (AVCC, 1.2/2.0/2.5-V REF, external) — not free-form.</span>
+    mcu.process(<span class="str">"ADC:REFERENCE BANANA"</span>)
+    <span class="kw">assert</span> <span class="fn">errors</span>(mcu) == <span class="num">1</span>
+
+<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">test_raw_respects_selected_reference</span>(self, mcu):
+    <span class="cm"># SLAU367P §34.2.1 Eq. 13: with VR+ = 1.2-V VREF, a 1.2-V input is full scale.</span>
+    mcu.process(<span class="str">"ADC:REFERENCE VREF"</span>)
+    mcu.inject_adc(<span class="num">0</span>, <span class="num">1.2</span>)
+    <span class="kw">assert</span> int(mcu.process(<span class="str">"ADC:CHANNEL0:RAW?"</span>)) == <span class="num">4095</span></code></pre>
+
+<p>Compliance moved from <strong>19.8% → 22.8%</strong>: <code>ADC:CHANNELn:RAW</code>, <code>ADC:CHn:RAW</code>, and <code>ADC:REFERENCE</code> all flipped NON_COMPLIANT → COMPLIANT. (<code>ADC:CONVERT</code> now scales correctly too but stays NON_COMPLIANT for unrelated reasons: it runs without <code>ADC12ENC</code> and returns <code>'0'</code> for nonexistent channels.)</p>
+
+<div class="callout">
+  <div class="callout-label">📌 One more detail: *RST</div>
+  The new VeREF+ pin state <code>self._veref_v</code> is reset to 1.2 in the <code>*RST</code> handler, alongside all other peripheral state. Any new device state you add must be reset there too — that's the *RST contract.
+</div>
